      "problem": "Express the equation $10^3 = 1\\,000$ using logarithmic notation.",
      "worked_solution": "The common logarithm of $a$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a = 10^x$ is equivalent to $\\log{a} = x$\n\nIf we compare $10^3 = 1\\,000$ with $10^x = a,$ we get that $a = 1\\,000$ and $x = 3.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation can be expressed as $\\log{1\\,000} = 3.$",
